From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Fri, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: rockchip: rock-pi-4a: cap SPI NOR frequency at 10 MHz

The upstream device tree declares spi-max-frequency = <108000000> for the
SPI NOR on ROCK Pi 4A. rk_spi clamps the rate to 50 MHz and divides the
198 MHz module clock by an even factor. At 19.8 MHz and above the data
from this flash arrives one bit late: the SFDP read returns 0xff and the
next probe fails:

  unrecognized JEDEC id bytes: ff, ff, ff
  Failed to initialize SPI flash at 1:0 (error -2)

At 9.9 MHz repeated probes and reads of the boot image are stable.

The rate cannot be lowered from the U-Boot shell: for a flash node from
the device tree, `sf probe <bus>:<cs> <speed>` probes the device at
spi-max-frequency before it applies the speed.

Cap the rate at 10 MHz in the U-Boot overlay: the value the device tree
had before Linux commit fa16d7a820e4 ("arm64: dts: rockchip: Increase
maximum frequency of SPI flash for ROCK Pi 4A/B/C"), and the one Armbian
uses in the kernel device tree.

Signed-off-by: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
---
 arch/arm/dts/rk3399-rock-pi-4a-u-boot.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-rock-pi-4a-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-rock-pi-4a-u-boot.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-rock-pi-4a-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-rock-pi-4a-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@

 &spi1 {
 	flash@0 {
+		spi-max-frequency = <10000000>;
 		bootph-pre-ram;
 		bootph-some-ram;
 	};
